# Badlands - Rares & Treasures companion (pack butler-routes-completionist, v1).
# An opportunistic sweep for the 6 confirmed flagged rares of the Badlands and
# its fixed world containers. Run it in its own Polestar tab at the end of
# the core route or standalone. EVERY goal is optional: a rare that is not
# up never holds the route. Spawn points and levels are the local Forever
# game data (questie-forever); signature drops are items whose SOLE dropper
# is the rare, and two of the six have none - they ship as kill goals with
# notes. One rare is a single confirmed point, so that step is a plain
# single-goto step (a loop needs at least two). No tame lines ship (the data
# has no tameability flag and the core guide carries no tame corroboration -
# see docs/companion-unverified.md). Respawn timers are unconfirmed anywhere,
# so none are stated. No rare in this guide is a giver, ender, or objective
# of any core-contracted quest (checked field by field - the 710/713/714 hits
# on 2850 are item-ID collisions, cleared - see
# docs/badlands-companions-inventory.md).
guide butler-routes-completionist/badlands-rares
title Badlands - Rares & Treasures
levels 28-40
zone Badlands
faction Alliance
category Collectibles
folder Companions
keywords badlands, rares, treasures, companions
coords live
version 1

step Siege Golem — the west

  zone map 1418

  loop
  goto 5.49,59.53
  goto 8.60,61.81
  goto 11.58,59.14
  goto 15.82,65.31
  goto 15.90,59.23
  goto 19.07,60.63
  goto 19.86,56.58
  goto 24.53,50.11
  goto 24.61,55.58
  goto 29.18,47.41
  goto 31.47,50.02
  goto 35.66,47.63
  goto 36.25,41.73
  goto 40.03,39.82
  kill 2749 optional
  collect 282561 "Siegebreaker's Blaster" optional
  note Level 40 rare elite working its 14 confirmed points in the west; its sole drop is the Siegebreaker's Blaster. No quest takes it.
  note Also drops ordinary greens; respawn timer unconfirmed.

